> f(x: u8) = match x { 0 => 1, 1 => 2 }
  note: match has no default arm: other values are outside the domain
> domain f
domain of f:
  x: u8, 0..255
  requires ((!(x == 0) && !(x == 1))) => an arm of match/piecewise covers the input
  defined at 2 of 256 points
  defined for: 0..1
  undefined e.g. at x=2; x=3; x=4; x=5
  over all 256 points of the domain
> range f
range of f -> int:
  1..2
  fits in u2
  undefined at 254 points
  over all 256 points of the domain
> g(x: real) = { x if x > 0 }
> domain g
domain of g:
  x: real (default [-10, 10])
  requires (!(x > 0)) => an arm of match/piecewise covers the input
  defined on (numerically, grid of 20001 over [-10, 10]):
    x in (0, 10]
> range g
range of g:
  [0.001, 10]   min at x ≈ 0.001, max at x ≈ 10
  undefined at 10001 of 20001 grid points
  grid of 20001 points over [-10, 10] (default; give x a range), extrema refined at critical points
